{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-13501-r4615190","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Azteca (Aztec-inspired Bean Soup)","sourcePageId":13501,"sourceRevision":"4615190","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:35:37Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Azteca%20(Aztec-inspired%20Bean%20Soup)&oldid=4615190","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:22:55.272Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for soup","Category:Recipes using black bean","Category:Recipes using corn","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using kidney bean","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes using onion","Category:Recipes using pequin chile","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Side dish recipes","Category:Vegan recipes","Category:Vegetarian recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"140a68345e907ec84f39e55492239a8ecc256f3f579eeed56c1fdf64627efee1","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Time = 30 minutes\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Side dishes|Side dishes]]\n\nThis is from Bob Uhl’s recipe for [http://latakia.dyndns.org/~ruhl/recipes/azteca Azteca] found on his [http://latakia.dyndns.org/~ruhl/recipes/bachelor bachelor recipes site]. It is inspired&mdash;in the loosest sense; it is ''not at all historical''&mdash;by the diet of the Aztecs, whence comes the name. It’s quite tasty and filling.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 1 can (~2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]]) [[Cookbook:Corn|corn]]\n* 1 can (~2 cups) [[cookbook:Kidney Bean|kidney beans]]\n* 1 can (~2 cups) [[cookbook:Black Bean|black beans]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]]\n* 4 cloves [[cookbook:garlic|garlic]], finely minced\n* 6 dried pequin [[cookbook:Chile Pepper|chiles]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* [[cookbook:Mustard Seed|Mustard seed]], [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]], and freshly-ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]], to taste\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Mix ingredients in pot.\n# Add three cans of water.\n# [[Cookbook:Boiling|Boil]] until done.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* For a historically accurate version, substitute pinto beans for kidney beans, use Mexican green onions, omit garlic and mustard seed, and substitute powdered chili pepper for black pepper. \n\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corn]]\n[[Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pequin chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using kidney bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes using black bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Azteca (Aztec-inspired Bean Soup)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 can (~2 cups) corn","sourceText":"1 can (~2 cups) corn","amountText":"1 can (~2 cups) corn","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 can (~2 cups) kidney beans","sourceText":"1 can (~2 cups) kidney beans","amountText":"1 can (~2 cups) kidney beans","amount":nu